          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The angular and paired-kernel checks reproduced their saved results exactly, apart from runtime. They support stopping the specific failed transfer and separate-coset positivity attempts.\n\nI also found a correction needed in 19: near a collision, the normalized negative witness grows, but the unnormalized quantity used for certification shrinks toward zero. And the computed collision times remain lower bounds for the global Newman constant unless all other zero pairs are controlled. Neither issue undermines 19’s value as a control screen.\n"
            ]
