          "create_time": 1791946688.751,
          "update_time": 1791946702.165,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "**I agree with most of the consolidation, but several closure claims are too strong.** I saved the [detailed review](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-2/brainstorm/reviews/PORTFOLIO_CLOSURE_REVIEW_CODEX_20261013.md).\n\nThe most important qualification concerns **02**. Its latest continuation establishes genuine progress: stable source recovery and an all-frequency positive correction bound. It also identifies why those results do not yet control the physical cancellation. **Pausing at that precise inequality is justified.** Treating 18’s Hecke formulation as having exhausted or replaced full imaginary Jacobi gluing is not established.\n\nMy recommended disposition is:\n\n| Programs | Assessment |\n|---|---|\n| 01, 02 | Pause with explicit reopening conditions. |\n| 04, 10, 11 → 06 | Agree with merging their related representations. |\n| 07, 15 → 18 | Agree organizationally; preserve their unfinished transport and compatibility obligations. |\n| 09 | Archive as a completed identity task, preserving the distinct 09-to-06 results and certified sector obstructions. |\n| 14, 16 | Make dormant. Their generic mechanisms are insufficient, but their proposed theta-specific tasks have not been ruled out. |\n| 17 | Archive the completed easy-cell calibration. It does not establish that topology cannot save work on harder cells. |\n| 18 | Allow one bounded continuation under its stopping condition. It has useful identities but no new complete sign. |\n| 19 | Keep as a shared control screen. |\n\nI also found two corrections needed in **19**: its tracked collision times do not establish the global Newman constant, and near collision the **raw negative certification margin shrinks**, even though the normalized ratio grows.\n\nThe remaining proposed roles—03/06 as destinations, 05 as a tool, 08 separately, and 12/13 as reading or bridge work—are reasonable.\n\nThe angular and paired-kernel replays matched their saved records exactly apart from runtime. **No folders were moved or closed.**"
            ]
          },
